      },
      "text": "UTILITARIANISM (Bentham, Mill, Sidgwick):\n  Good = happiness/welfare/utility; maximize total aggregate\n  Jeremy Bentham: \"the greatest happiness for the greatest number\"\n  Act utilitarianism: each act evaluated by its actual consequences\n  Rule utilitarianism: act according to rules whose general acceptance maximizes utility\n    (addresses objections about extreme cases; more rule-following behavior)"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-ETHICS.md#019",
      "path": [
        "05-ETHICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
